Package: cosetsampling
Type: Package
Title: Exactly Balanced Sampling with Affine Flats and Coset Designs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Mohamed", "Laib", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "laib.med@gmail.com")
Description: Exactly balanced sampling designs for frames whose units are indexed by
    a vector space over a prime field, such as complete factorial frames and square
    grids of prime side, stratified by cosets of subspaces (margins, cross-classifications,
    rows, columns and wrapped diagonals). A coset design draws a random admissible
    direction and a random set of cosets of it; every sample is exactly balanced on all
    the stratifications. The package lists and samples admissible directions, builds coset
    designs (uniform, user-given or minimax mixtures of directions), draws samples, and
    gives first- and second-order inclusion probabilities, spectral weights, exact
    variances and design effects, worst-case factors, and the random-group and regression
    variance estimators. Diagnostics measure the balance and the main-effect weight share
    of samples from any design, such as the cube method, and the corresponding lower
    bound on the worst-case variance.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
